stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Loading: expand
    Loading --> Ready: valid latest response
    Loading --> Error: malformed or failed response
    Error --> Loading: explicit refresh
    Ready --> Loading: refresh or server filters
    Ready --> Ready: apply valid inclusive window or deal type
    Ready --> Invalid: invalid or reversed draft
    Invalid --> Ready: correct or clear window
    Invalid --> Loading: refresh preserves applied window
    Loading --> Loading: newer refresh supersedes pending read
    Ready --> Ready: ignore stale completion
    Loading --> Idle: clear or pagehide
    Ready --> Idle: clear or pagehide
    Loading --> Retired: session invalidation
    Ready --> Retired: session invalidation
    Retired --> Retired: refuse old controls and late completion
    Idle --> Disposed: dispose
    Loading --> Disposed: dispose
    Ready --> Disposed: dispose
    Disposed --> Disposed: refuse old controls and late completion

%% System design written before implementation.
%% Data shape: immutable Profile[] owns full-history counts and dated evidence. CloseWindow owns two validated inclusive bounds. Draft strings and validation message never replace the applied CloseWindow on refusal.
%% Architecture: the existing mount owns selection, rendering and lifecycle. Client owns the existing bounded authenticated read. No new public interface or persistence.
%% Capacity: one linear pass over loaded evidence per local edit, at most 1000 groups. At 10x evidence the first bottleneck is DOM rendering, not network. No fan-out or N+1 reads.
%% Cache: one loaded snapshot. Refresh evicts visible evidence while pending or failed. Latest epoch replaces snapshot; window survives refresh; clear, retirement and disposal evict selection.
%% Consistency: full-history counts stay authoritative. Matching evidence is derived locally; never infer client counts. Invalid input retains the last valid view.
%% Availability: one explicit read per expand, refresh or server submit. Existing client deadline applies. No retry loop. Failure hides data and offers explicit refresh; auth retirement prevents future reads.
%% Async lifetime: no queue; epoch and active lifecycle refuse stale completion. Disposal unmounts and removes listeners.
%% External proof: same-origin read-only transport, one total deadline, bounded reads; acquisition failure is insufficient evidence. Borrowed browser stays open. Owned handles close, including late acquisitions.
%% Writes, idempotency keys, storage scaling and load spread: n/a, local projection only.
%% Throughput: blocking contract and baseline tests first; one owner because UI and proof share one behavior; no independent agents or shared mutable state.

state "Production proof" as Proof {
    [*] --> Connecting
    Connecting --> Insufficient: connection rejected or context absent
    Connecting --> Acquiring: signed-in context available
    Acquiring --> Insufficient: page acquisition rejected
    Acquiring --> Observing: page acquired before deadline
    Acquiring --> Draining: deadline expires with page pending
    Observing --> Draining: pass, assertion failure, or deadline
    Draining --> Disconnected: pending acquisition settles and owned page closes
    Disconnected --> [*]: borrowed browser and prior tabs remain open
}

%% Proof data shape: one pending page promise and one memoized cleanup promise per borrowed connection.
%% Cleanup keeps the CDP transport alive until the pending page settles and closes, then disconnects once.
%% No new interface, cache, queue, storage, external request, or retry. Existing budgets and release checks remain.
%% Evidence compares exact link labels, time text, datetime attributes and identities against the independently observed response.
